          "message": "feat(tenant): multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant resource quotas (#3365) (#3780)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements **multi-tenant namespaces with per-tenant resource\nisolation** (#3365) — serving many isolated logical databases from one\nprocess.\n\n**Design: instance-per-tenant.** A new `TenantManager` owns **one\nfully-separate `AletheiaDB` per tenant**. Because the instances share no\nstorage, no locks, and no ID space, the hard-isolation guarantees fall\nout *by construction* rather than from leak-prone per-query filtering:\n\n- **Hard data isolation** — no query surface\n(get/property/traversal/k-NN/`AS OF`/changefeed/errors) can return\nanother tenant's data; a handle only ever touches its own instance.\n- **Temporal invariants compose** — each tenant *is* a single-tenant DB,\nso valid/tx-time, WAL durability, and crash recovery are byte-for-byte\nsingle-tenant; independent `.albk` backup/restore per tenant.\n- **Blast-radius containment** — one tenant hitting a\nquota/erroring/being deleted touches only its own map entry + directory;\nseparate lock graphs.\n- **ID/business-key collision is harmless.**\n\n## What's included\n\n**Core (`src/core/tenant.rs`):** `TenantId` (validated —\n**lowercase-only + FS/Windows-safe** so a case-insensitive-filesystem\ndirectory collision, e.g. `Acme` vs `acme` sharing one WAL, is\nimpossible by construction), `TenantQuota`, `TenantUsage`, `TenantInfo`,\n`QuotaDimension`, `TenantError` (wired into `Error::Tenant`).\n\n**Runtime (`src/tenant/`):** `TenantManager` (`new_ephemeral` / durable\n`open(root)` with a quarantine-on-corrupt registry sidecar;\n`create_tenant`/`get_tenant`/`get_tenant_info`/`list_tenants`/`tenant_usage`/`set_tenant_quota`/`delete_tenant`/`restore_tenant`),\n`TenantHandle` (bind a session to one tenant; isolated reads via `db()`,\nquota-enforced `create_*`/`delete_*`, tenant-scoped `mcp_server()`).\n\n**Quotas:** `max_nodes`/`max_edges` enforced **precisely** via an atomic\nreservation taken-before-write / released-on-failure (never a partial\nwrite, never a race past the cap; decrements saturate so drift can never\nwrap and brick a tenant). `max_vector_index_bytes`/`max_storage_bytes`\nenforced **best-effort** against O(1) estimators. A breach →\n`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (non-retriable,\n`details:{tenant,dimension,current,limit}`) on **both** the MCP and HTTP\n#3234 envelopes; lifecycle → `INVALID_ARGUMENT`/`NOT_FOUND`/`CONFLICT`.\n\n**Usage accounting:** O(1) counters, metering-suitable. **Single-tenant\ndefault untouched, zero overhead.**\n\n## Tests (all green)\n\n`tests/multi_tenant_isolation.rs` + `src/tenant/tests.rs` (26 unit + 6\nintegration): cross-tenant leak suite, concurrent soak (**0 leaks, 0\nquota-bypass** across 10 tenants), noisy-neighbor blast-radius,\nprecise/no-partial-write quota enforcement, counter-underflow\nregression, per-tenant backup/restore independence, durable restart,\ncorrupt-registry quarantine, MCP tenant-scoping, and #3234 error mapping\non both surfaces.\n\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` → clean\n- `cargo fmt --all` applied\n\n## Method\n\nPlanned with brainstorming / reverse-brainstorming / six-hats; built TDD\n(red→green→refactor); reviewed by three independent agents\n(concurrency/quota, isolation/leak-surface, API/idiom) with all findings\nfixed — notably the lowercase-id fix (case-insensitive-FS collision) and\nsaturating decrements (counter underflow).\n\n## v1 scope / follow-ups\n\nRust-API core + MCP tenant-scoping + #3234 error wiring. Documented\ncaveats that compose on this core: the string interner is\n**process-global** (a cross-tenant capacity/DoS caveat — data *values*\nare never shared; per-tenant interners are a follow-up), and admin\n*tool* wiring on the MCP/HTTP/CLI surfaces plus #3350 identity→tenant\nbinding are coordinated follow-ups. See `docs/guides/multi-tenancy.md`.\n\nCloses #3365 (core); surface-admin + identity binding tracked as\nfollow-ups.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014vwQb3aLknTzZW5K8Wd9YN\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_014vwQb3aLknTzZW5K8Wd9YN)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
